Devirtualize a virtual or interface call when every class the receiver can have resolves it to the
same method (NativeAOT).

impDevirtualizeCall gives up on a receiver whose type it knows only as an interface or a non-final
class, and guarded devirtualization then type-tests at most a few exact classes (getExactClasses,
from ILC's whole-program view). A class hierarchy that implements an interface once, at its root -
a configuration base class with one subclass per variant - has more classes than that but one target
per method. impDevirtualizeToUniqueTarget asks getExactClasses for up to 64 classes, resolves the
method on each, and when all agree on one method (no value classes, no shared generic code, no
instantiation argument) turns the call into a direct call to it, with an explicit null check when the
receiver may be null. The direct call can then be inlined.

Nethermind stateless guest on ZisK, with IReleaseSpec implemented only by ReleaseSpec and its fork
subclasses in the guest (NethermindEth/nethermind companion change): interface dispatch cells
1,160 -> 643;
  block 26055159 steps 55,887,466 -> 55,069,856 (-1.46%), cost 9,278,440,342 -> 9,199,861,389 (-0.85%)
  block 26112793 steps 130,709,033 -> 129,614,991 (-0.84%), cost 19,170,876,078 -> 19,067,586,567 (-0.54%)
